ent is retrieved starting from the specified Source Equipment, and according to the specified Material or Material Group. The returned list is empty when no destination Equipment handles the specified Material or Material Group.","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"The list of the natural identifiers of the Equipment that are part of the Equipment Flow.The list of Equipment is retrieved starting from the specified Source Equipment, and according to the specified Material or Material Group. The returned list is empty when no destination Equipment handles the specified Material or Material Group."},"SystemAnnotations":[{"$id":"2746","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"Optional","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Optional","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Optional"}],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"EquipmentNIds","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"EquipmentNIds"},{"$id":"2747","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"AS","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"AS","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"AS"},{"$id":"2748","$type":"DslCommandPropertyTypeTree","Children":[{"$id":"2749","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"list of","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"list of","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"list of"},{"$id":"2750","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"string","FullInfo":"String","InfoMap":{"$id":"2751","FullIdObj":{"$id":"2752","$type":"IdentificableTypeSystem","Name":"string","FullInfo":"String","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"2752"},"Children":[],"Name":"SimpleSystemTypeNode","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"Line":567,"CharPositionInLine":29,"_text":"string","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"string"}],"Name":"CommandPropertyType","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]}],"Name":"PropertyTree","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]}]}],"Name":"Output declaration commands","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]}],"Name":"CommandDeclaration","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]},{"$id":"2753","$type":"DslCommandDeclarationTree","HasInput":true,"HasOutput":true,"Children":[{"$id":"2754","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"COMMAND","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"COMMAND","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"COMMAND"},{"$id":"2755","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"SplitMTU","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIMaterial_OP.OPModel.Commands.SplitMTU","InfoMap":{"$id":"2756","FullIdObj":{"$id":"2757","$type":"IdentificableObject","Guid":"410e6d45-45a2-4d66-8680-7910dcb038aa","Name":"SplitMTU","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIMaterial_OP.OPModel.Commands.SplitMTU","TypeResolved":"","_project":{"$ref":"12"},"_domain":{"$ref":"366"}}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"2757"},"Children":[],"Name":"CommandName","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"Documentation":{"$id":"2758","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"Takes part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity (source quantity) to create a new MTU, which inherits Material, Material Lot, State Machine and Properties from the source. If an MTU Template is specified as input, the new MTU inherits its state machine and properties.\r\nIf no quantity is specified as input (SplitQuantity.QuantityValue =0 or SplitQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that must be taken must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure of the source quantity. It is possible to use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n1. Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the quantity given as input.\r\n2. Creates a new Material Tracking Unit with the quantity given as input. The new Material Tracking Unit inherits the Material, Material Lot and Properties of the source and can be located in the same location (Equipment or Material Tracking Unit Aggregate) as the source.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, if some checks on input parameters fail:\r\n* Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n* Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n* Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the SplitQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with the source quantity.\r\n* Error -12103: the quantity specified as input exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, during its execution:\r\n* Error -12104: If the creation of the new Material Tracking Unit fails.\r\n* Error -12105: If a failure occurs when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","FullInfo":"Takes part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity (source quantity) to create a new MTU, which inherits Material, Material Lot, State Machine and Properties from the source. If an MTU Template is specified as input, the new MTU inherits its state machine and properties.\r\nIf no quantity is specified as input (SplitQuantity.QuantityValue =0 or SplitQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that must be taken must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure of the source quantity. It is possible to use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n1. Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the quantity given as input.\r\n2. Creates a new Material Tracking Unit with the quantity given as input. The new Material Tracking Unit inherits the Material, Material Lot and Properties of the source and can be located in the same location (Equipment or Material Tracking Unit Aggregate) as the source.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, if some checks on input parameters fail:\r\n* Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n* Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n* Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the SplitQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with the source quantity.\r\n* Error -12103: the quantity specified as input exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, during its execution:\r\n* Error -12104: If the creation of the new Material Tracking Unit fails.\r\n* Error -12105: If a failure occurs when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","InfoMap":{"$id":"2759","FullIdObj":{"$id":"2760","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"Takes part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity (source quantity) to create a new MTU, which inherits Material, Material Lot, State Machine and Properties from the source. If an MTU Template is specified as input, the new MTU inherits its state machine and properties.\r\nIf no quantity is specified as input (SplitQuantity.QuantityValue =0 or SplitQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that must be taken must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure of the source quantity. It is possible to use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n1. Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the quantity given as input.\r\n2. Creates a new Material Tracking Unit with the quantity given as input. The new Material Tracking Unit inherits the Material, Material Lot and Properties of the source and can be located in the same location (Equipment or Material Tracking Unit Aggregate) as the source.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, if some checks on input parameters fail:\r\n* Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n* Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n* Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the SplitQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with the source quantity.\r\n* Error -12103: the quantity specified as input exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, during its execution:\r\n* Error -12104: If the creation of the new Material Tracking Unit fails.\r\n* Error -12105: If a failure occurs when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","FullInfo":"Takes part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity (source quantity) to create a new MTU, which inherits Material, Material Lot, State Machine and Properties from the source. If an MTU Template is specified as input, the new MTU inherits its state machine and properties.\r\nIf no quantity is specified as input (SplitQuantity.QuantityValue =0 or SplitQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that must be taken must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure of the source quantity. It is possible to use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n1. Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the quantity given as input.\r\n2. Creates a new Material Tracking Unit with the quantity given as input. The new Material Tracking Unit inherits the Material, Material Lot and Properties of the source and can be located in the same location (Equipment or Material Tracking Unit Aggregate) as the source.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, if some checks on input parameters fail:\r\n* Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n* Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n* Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the SplitQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with the source quantity.\r\n* Error -12103: the quantity specified as input exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, during its execution:\r\n* Error -12104: If the creation of the new Material Tracking Unit fails.\r\n* Error -12105: If a failure occurs when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"2760"},"Children":[],"Name":"Documentation","SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Takes part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity (source quantity) to create a new MTU, which inherits Material, Material Lot, State Machine and Properties from the source. If an MTU Template is specified as input, the new MTU inherits its state machine and properties.\r\nIf no quantity is specified as input (SplitQuantity.QuantityValue =0 or SplitQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that must be taken must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure of the source quantity. It is possible to use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n1. Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the quantity given as input.\r\n2. Creates a new Material Tracking Unit with the quantity given as input. The new Material Tracking Unit inherits the Material, Material Lot and Properties of the source and can be located in the same location (Equipment or Material Tracking Unit Aggregate) as the source.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, if some checks on input parameters fail:\r\n* Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n* Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n* Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the SplitQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with the source quantity.\r\n* Error -12103: the quantity specified as input exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, during its execution:\r\n* Error -12104: If the creation of the new Material Tracking Unit fails.\r\n* Error -12105: If a failure occurs when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Takes part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity (source quantity) to create a new MTU, which inherits Material, Material Lot, State Machine and Properties from the source. If an MTU Template is specified as input, the new MTU inherits its state machine and properties.\r\nIf no quantity is specified as input (SplitQuantity.QuantityValue =0 or SplitQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that must be taken must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure of the source quantity. It is possible to use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n1. Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the quantity given as input.\r\n2. Creates a new Material Tracking Unit with the quantity given as input. The new Material Tracking Unit inherits the Material, Material Lot and Properties of the source and can be located in the same location (Equipment or Material Tracking Unit Aggregate) as the source.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, if some checks on input parameters fail:\r\n* Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n* Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n* Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the SplitQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with the source quantity.\r\n* Error -12103: the quantity specified as input exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, during its execution:\r\n* Error -12104: If the creation of the new Material Tracking Unit fails.\r\n* Error -12105: If a failure occurs when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity."},"SystemAnnotations":[{"$id":"2761","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"Protected","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Protected","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Protected"}],"CustomAnnotations":[{"$id":"2762","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"@Guid(410e6d45-45a2-4d66-8680-7910dcb038aa)","FullInfo":"@Guid(410e6d45-45a2-4d66-8680-7910dcb038aa)","InfoMap":{"$id":"2763","FullIdObj":{"$id":"2764","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"@Guid(410e6d45-45a2-4d66-8680-7910dcb038aa)","FullInfo":"@Guid(410e6d45-45a2-4d66-8680-7910dcb038aa)","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"2764"},"Children":[],"Name":"CustomAnnotation","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"@Guid(410e6d45-45a2-4d66-8680-7910dcb038aa)","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"@Guid(410e6d45-45a2-4d66-8680-7910dcb038aa)"}],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"SplitMTU","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"SplitMTU"},{"$id":"2765","$type":"DslCommandInputDeclarationTree","Children":[{"$id":"2766","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"WITH","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"WITH","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"WITH"},{"$id":"2767","$type":"DslCommandPropertyCollectionTree","Name":"InputProperties","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[]