:[],"_text":"COMMAND","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"COMMAND"},{"$id":"2981","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"ConsumeMTU","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIMaterial_OP.OPModel.Commands.ConsumeMTU","InfoMap":{"$id":"2982","FullIdObj":{"$id":"2983","$type":"IdentificableObject","Guid":"54d16ed8-9f38-4cfc-b206-4b9a9bf55f7d","Name":"ConsumeMTU","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIMaterial_OP.OPModel.Commands.ConsumeMTU","TypeResolved":"","_project":{"$ref":"12"},"_domain":{"$ref":"366"}}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"2983"},"Children":[],"Name":"CommandName","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"Documentation":{"$id":"2984","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"A part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity is detached in order to be consumed in the production process.\r\nIf the input quantity is not specified (ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = 0 or ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that is going to be decreased must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure as the Material Tracking Unit quantity. You can use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n*Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the given input quantity.\r\n*Converts the UoM of the input quantity if different from MTU UoM, but belonging to the same dimension.\r\n*When completing,  the command rises the event MTUOperationCompleted with the info about the quantity that has been decreased and the info about source MTU.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, **if some checks on input parameters fail**:\r\n*Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n*Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n*Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with that of source quantity.\r\n*Error -12103: the specified input quantity exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following **error codes, during its execution**:\r\n*Error -12105: a failure is occurred when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","FullInfo":"A part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity is detached in order to be consumed in the production process.\r\nIf the input quantity is not specified (ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = 0 or ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that is going to be decreased must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure as the Material Tracking Unit quantity. You can use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n*Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the given input quantity.\r\n*Converts the UoM of the input quantity if different from MTU UoM, but belonging to the same dimension.\r\n*When completing,  the command rises the event MTUOperationCompleted with the info about the quantity that has been decreased and the info about source MTU.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, **if some checks on input parameters fail**:\r\n*Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n*Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n*Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with that of source quantity.\r\n*Error -12103: the specified input quantity exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following **error codes, during its execution**:\r\n*Error -12105: a failure is occurred when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","InfoMap":{"$id":"2985","FullIdObj":{"$id":"2986","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"A part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity is detached in order to be consumed in the production process.\r\nIf the input quantity is not specified (ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = 0 or ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that is going to be decreased must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure as the Material Tracking Unit quantity. You can use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n*Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the given input quantity.\r\n*Converts the UoM of the input quantity if different from MTU UoM, but belonging to the same dimension.\r\n*When completing,  the command rises the event MTUOperationCompleted with the info about the quantity that has been decreased and the info about source MTU.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, **if some checks on input parameters fail**:\r\n*Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n*Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n*Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with that of source quantity.\r\n*Error -12103: the specified input quantity exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following **error codes, during its execution**:\r\n*Error -12105: a failure is occurred when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","FullInfo":"A part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity is detached in order to be consumed in the production process.\r\nIf the input quantity is not specified (ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = 0 or ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that is going to be decreased must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure as the Material Tracking Unit quantity. You can use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n*Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the given input quantity.\r\n*Converts the UoM of the input quantity if different from MTU UoM, but belonging to the same dimension.\r\n*When completing,  the command rises the event MTUOperationCompleted with the info about the quantity that has been decreased and the info about source MTU.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, **if some checks on input parameters fail**:\r\n*Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n*Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n*Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with that of source quantity.\r\n*Error -12103: the specified input quantity exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following **error codes, during its execution**:\r\n*Error -12105: a failure is occurred when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"2986"},"Children":[],"Name":"Documentation","SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"A part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity is detached in order to be consumed in the production process.\r\nIf the input quantity is not specified (ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = 0 or ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that is going to be decreased must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure as the Material Tracking Unit quantity. You can use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n*Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the given input quantity.\r\n*Converts the UoM of the input quantity if different from MTU UoM, but belonging to the same dimension.\r\n*When completing,  the command rises the event MTUOperationCompleted with the info about the quantity that has been decreased and the info about source MTU.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, **if some checks on input parameters fail**:\r\n*Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n*Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n*Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with that of source quantity.\r\n*Error -12103: the specified input quantity exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following **error codes, during its execution**:\r\n*Error -12105: a failure is occurred when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity.","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"A part of the source Material Tracking Unit quantity is detached in order to be consumed in the production process.\r\nIf the input quantity is not specified (ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = 0 or ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue = NULL), the entire source Material Tracking Unit quantity is taken, setting the source MTU quantity to zero.\r\nThe quantity that is going to be decreased must be expressed with the same Unit of Measure as the Material Tracking Unit quantity. You can use a different Unit of Measure only if it belongs to the same dimension.\r\nThe command:\r\n*Decreases the source Material Tracking Unit quantity by the given input quantity.\r\n*Converts the UoM of the input quantity if different from MTU UoM, but belonging to the same dimension.\r\n*When completing,  the command rises the event MTUOperationCompleted with the info about the quantity that has been decreased and the info about source MTU.\r\nThe command may return the following error codes, **if some checks on input parameters fail**:\r\n*Error -12100: the MTU, identified by NId, does not exist.\r\n*Error -12101: no quantity is specified for source MTU (NULL or zero).\r\n*Error -12102: the Unit of Measure used to express the ConsumeQuantity.QuantityValue is not compatible with that of source quantity.\r\n*Error -12103: the specified input quantity exceeds the source MTU quantity.\r\nThe command may return the following **error codes, during its execution**:\r\n*Error -12105: a failure is occurred when decreasing the source Material Tracking Unit quantity."},"SystemAnnotations":[{"$id":"2987","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"Protected","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Protected","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Protected"}],"CustomAnnotations":[{"$id":"2988","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"@Guid(54d16ed8-9f38-4cfc-b206-4b9a9bf55f7d)","FullInfo":"@Guid(54d16ed8-9f38-4cfc-b206-4b9a9bf55f7d)","InfoMap":{"$id":"2989","FullIdObj":{"$id":"2990","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"@Guid(54d16ed8-9f38-4cfc-b206-4b9a9bf55f7d)","FullInfo":"@Guid(54d16ed8-9f38-4cfc-b206-4b9a9bf55f7d)","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"2990"},"Children":[],"Name":"CustomAnnotation","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"@Guid(54d16ed8-9f38-4cfc-b206-4b9a9bf55f7d)","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"@Guid(54d16ed8-9f38-4cfc-b206-4b9a9bf55f7d)"}],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"ConsumeMTU","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"ConsumeMTU"},{"$id":"2991","$type":"DslCommandInputDeclarationTree","Children":[{"$id":"2992","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"WITH","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"WITH","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"WITH"},{"$id":"2993","$type":"DslCommandPropertyCollectionTree","Name":"InputProperties","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"ChildrenList":[{"$id":"2994","$type":"DslCommandPropertyTree","Children":[{"$id":"2995","$type":"DslTerminalNode"