 purpose is to be implemented via a post action to customize the logic for deleting a Material Tracking Unit, based on the specific scenario.\r\nThe command also allows for defining a Material in input, in case there is the need to change the identity of the MTU, prior to remove it.\r\nCustom Fields are also foreseen for further customization.\r\n","FullInfo":"This is an empty command with the same signature as the DeleteMaterialTrackingUnit command. Its purpose is to be implemented via a post action to customize the logic for deleting a Material Tracking Unit, based on the specific scenario.\r\nThe command also allows for defining a Material in input, in case there is the need to change the identity of the MTU, prior to remove it.\r\nCustom Fields are also foreseen for further customization.\r\n","InfoMap":{"$id":"4704","FullIdObj":{"$id":"4705","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"This is an empty command with the same signature as the DeleteMaterialTrackingUnit command. Its purpose is to be implemented via a post action to customize the logic for deleting a Material Tracking Unit, based on the specific scenario.\r\nThe command also allows for defining a Material in input, in case there is the need to change the identity of the MTU, prior to remove it.\r\nCustom Fields are also foreseen for further customization.\r\n","FullInfo":"This is an empty command with the same signature as the DeleteMaterialTrackingUnit command. Its purpose is to be implemented via a post action to customize the logic for deleting a Material Tracking Unit, based on the specific scenario.\r\nThe command also allows for defining a Material in input, in case there is the need to change the identity of the MTU, prior to remove it.\r\nCustom Fields are also foreseen for further customization.\r\n","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"4705"},"Children":[],"Name":"Documentation","SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"This is an empty command with the same signature as the DeleteMaterialTrackingUnit command. Its purpose is to be implemented via a post action to customize the logic for deleting a Material Tracking Unit, based on the specific scenario.\r\nThe command also allows for defining a Material in input, in case there is the need to change the identity of the MTU, prior to remove it.\r\nCustom Fields are also foreseen for further customization.\r\n","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"This is an empty command with the same signature as the DeleteMaterialTrackingUnit command. Its purpose is to be implemented via a post action to customize the logic for deleting a Material Tracking Unit, based on the specific scenario.\r\nThe command also allows for defining a Material in input, in case there is the need to change the identity of the MTU, prior to remove it.\r\nCustom Fields are also foreseen for further customization.\r\n"},"SystemAnnotations":[{"$id":"4706","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"Protected","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Protected","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Protected"}],"CustomAnnotations":[{"$id":"4707","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"@Guid(f64cd257-948d-490d-b0cd-9270a906a297)","FullInfo":"@Guid(f64cd257-948d-490d-b0cd-9270a906a297)","InfoMap":{"$id":"4708","FullIdObj":{"$id":"4709","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"@Guid(f64cd257-948d-490d-b0cd-9270a906a297)","FullInfo":"@Guid(f64cd257-948d-490d-b0cd-9270a906a297)","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"4709"},"Children":[],"Name":"CustomAnnotation","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"363"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"@Guid(f64cd257-948d-490d-b0cd-9270a906a297)","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"@Guid(f64cd257-948d-490d-b0cd-9270a906a297)"}],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"DeleteMaterialTrackingUnit_Interface","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"DeleteMaterial